    <statement><p>Suppose <m>f \left( x, y \right) = \frac{x}{y}</m>, <m>P = \left( 0, -3 \right)</m> and <m>\mathbf{v} = -3 \mathbf{i}  - 1 \mathbf{j}</m>.</p>
<p>A. Find the gradient of <m>f</m>.</p>
<p><m>(\nabla f)(x,y) =</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0001"/> <m>\mathbf{i} +</m> <fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0002"/> <m>\mathbf{j}</m></p>
<p>Note: Your answers should be expressions of x and y; e.g. <lq/>3x - 4y<rq/></p>
<p>B. Find the gradient of <m>f</m> at the point <m>P</m>.</p>
<p><m>\left( \nabla f \right) \left( P \right) =</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0003"/> <m>\mathbf{i} +</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0004"/> <m>\mathbf{j}</m></p>
<p>Note: Your answers should be numbers</p>
<p>C. Find the directional derivative of <m>f</m> at <m>P</m> in the direction of <m>\mathbf{v}</m>.</p>
<p><m>(D_{\mathbf{u}} f)(P) =</m> <fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0005"/></p>
<p>Note: Your answer should be a number</p>
<p>D. Find the maximum rate of change of <m>f</m> at <m>P</m>.</p>
<p><fillin characters="50" name="AnSwEr0006"/></p>
<p>Note: Your answer should be a number</p>
<p>E. Find the (unit) direction vector <m>\mathbf{w}</m> in which the maximum rate of change occurs
at <m>P</m>.</p>
<p><m>\mathbf{w} =</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0007"/> <m>\mathbf{i} +</m> <fillin characters="30" name="AnSwEr0008"/> <m>\mathbf{j}</m></p>
<p>Note: Your answers should be numbers</p>
</statement>
